{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>A virgin of his own people.</b> Why was this necessary, seeing that it already stated, ״והוא אשה בבתוליה יקח״? Rather, from here we learn that it is forbidden for the High Priest to betroth by intercourse, because the conclusion of intercourse effects acquisition, and when he acquires her at the conclusion of intercourse she is no longer a virgin, for she is a בעולה (non-virgin) of his own making, and the High Priest is warned against a בעולה of his own making just as against a בעולה of others, and this is what it says: ״כי אם בתולה מעמיו יקח״ — but not a בעולה; and this is a negative injunction derived from an affirmative command, as is found in the first chapter of Kiddushin."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:35.816642565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}